.Dd August 14, 2026
.Dt FILEES-RECOVERY-ENTRY 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm filees-recovery-entry
.Nd serve FileES realm-removal archives for one operation
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the set-id session entry for
.Sy _filees-recovery .
A second image of the same binary is installed as
.Pa /usr/local/libexec/filees/filees-recovery-authorize
.Pq owner root , group wheel , mode 0555
because
.Xr sshd 8
requires every
.Ic AuthorizedKeysCommand
component to be root-owned.
Key lookup and session service are therefore distinct executables.
.Pp
The client presents a per-operation Ed25519 recovery key from the
.Pa .fkr
kit written during realm removal.
The authorise helper emits a restricted key line bound to that one
operation ID and refuses it after
.Ic download_until .
The session protocol is exactly two verbs:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
list <operation_id>
get  <operation_id> <archive_id>
.Ed
.Pp
The entry is read-only
.Pq Cm stdio rpath
and never sees a private key.
The key grants no SVN access, no shell and no other operation.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr filees-admin 8 ,
.Xr filees 7
